{"chapter": "sites-cohomology", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "0CJZ", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$p : \\mathcal{S} \\to \\mathcal{C}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{stacks-lemma-gerbe-abelian-auts}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent", "STRUCT_0002": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0003": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:cc1ea641e8e8e02d36b49b1b6f347c9f0ad6a7e04138b8f4400aa94270b0af50", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:b371eb362926bf0186774e2a98d9d6bcf9463825ffb24d64cae23ecf77842187", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nLet <MATH_0001> be a gerbe over a site\nall of whose automorphism groups are commutative. In this situation\nthe first and second cohomology groups of the sheaf of automorphisms\n(Stacks, Lemma <REF_0001>)\ncontrols the existence of objects.\n\n<STRUCT_0002><STRUCT_0003>\nThe following lemma will be made obsolete by a more complete\ndiscussion of this relationship we will add in the future.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:0712599180e056984f5d329126f974003c38f402eddd8ce17b50614acd69f918", "unit_id": "tag:0CJZ:prose-0001"}
